{number: 72}
{title: Living for Jesus}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Living for Jesus a life that is true,
Striving to [Bb] please Him in [F] all that I do;
Yielding al-[Bb] legiance, glad-hearted and [F] free,
This is the [G7] pathway of blessing for [C7] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [F] Jesus, Lord and Savior, I give myself to Thee,
For [Bb] Thou, in Thine a-[C7] tonement, didst [F] give Thyself for me;
I [F] own no other Master, my [Bb] heart shall be Thy throne;
My [F] life I give, hence-[C7] forth to live, O Christ, for Thee a-[F] lone.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Living for Jesus Who died in my place,
Bearing on [Bb] Calv'ry my [F] sin and disgrace;
Such love con-[Bb] strains me to answer His [F] call,
Follow His [G7] leading and give Him my [C7] all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Living for Jesus through earth's little while,
My dearest [Bb] treasure, the [F] light of His smile;
Seeking the [Bb] lost ones He died to re-[F] deem,
Bringing the [G7] weary to find rest in [C7] Him.
{end_of_verse}
